{"id":"src/app/api/live/markets/route.ts","pkg":"src/app/api","kind":"route","lines":44,"commentLines":8,"header":["Sensex, Nifty and the watch list. I read nothing from the caller. The source (Yahoo Finance's public chart feed) turns away anyone who asks too fast, so I ask GENTLY: one symbol at a time with a pause between, each symbol kept five minutes in the server's memory (only the symbols that have gone stale are asked again), and at the first \"too many requests\" I stop asking and show what I have (the last good figures of the others, with their own times). A refresh therefore fills the card up over a few minutes rather than failing all at once. Only when no symbol has ever been fetched is it an error. When Yahoo does not answer, a symbol falls back to its last good quote (memory, then the saved copy in public.market_quote) and the answer says which ones and when they were received (src/lib/live/marketService.ts)."],"symbols":[{"name":"dynamic","kind":"constant","exported":true,"line":16,"sig":"const dynamic = \"force-dynamic\"","type":"","doc":[],"members":[],"items":0,"id":"975f032f48-dynamic","usedBy":[]},{"name":"maxDuration","kind":"constant","exported":true,"line":17,"sig":"const maxDuration = 30","type":"","doc":[],"members":[],"items":0,"id":"975f032f48-maxDuration","usedBy":[]},{"name":"chartUrl","kind":"function","exported":false,"line":19,"async":false,"sig":"const chartUrl = (symbol: string) =>","params":[{"name":"symbol","type":"string","optional":false,"rest":false,"def":""}],"returns":"","doc":[],"paramDocs":{},"returnDoc":"","id":"975f032f48-chartUrl","usedBy":[]},{"name":"sleep","kind":"function","exported":false,"line":20,"async":false,"sig":"const sleep = (ms: number) =>","params":[{"name":"ms","type":"number","optional":false,"rest":false,"def":""}],"returns":"","doc":[],"paramDocs":{},"returnDoc":"","id":"975f032f48-sleep","usedBy":[]},{"name":"savedCopy","kind":"function","exported":false,"isDefault":false,"async":true,"line":22,"sig":"a